"""Generate thesis notes only from saved commands/artifacts, never invented metrics."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
facts=json.loads((ROOT/'docs/evidence/phase5/project-facts.json').read_text())
benchmark=json.loads((ROOT/'docs/evidence/phase2/benchmark/benchmark.json').read_text())
validation=json.loads((ROOT/'docs/evidence/phase3/model-validation.json').read_text())
lines=['# Final-year report notes: verified facts and caveats','','Generated by `python -B tools/report_notes.py` from saved outputs. Copy the caveats with the numbers.','','## Implemented system','','React/Vite frontend, FastAPI backend, SQLite/SQLAlchemy, ONNX Runtime. Four classes in order: Face Mask, Helmet, Person, Safety Vest. Centered letterbox/RGB/pixels divided by 255, per-class NMS and original-coordinate reversal. Evidence: `backend/detection/model.py`, isolated detector tests, and `docs/evidence/phase3/model-validation.json`.','','The runtime contract is '+str(validation['input_shape'])+' input and '+str(validation['output_shape'])+' output without embedded NMS. Model SHA-256: `'+validation['model_sha256']+'`. The five-image validation command is saved in that JSON. Metadata declares class order; exact export-to-training-run provenance is not established.','','## Dataset facts','','Source command: `python -B tools/project_facts.py`; output `docs/evidence/phase5/project-facts.json`. Counts below are a read-only scan of the original local YOLO-format dataset, not counts of the augmented dataset.','','| Split | Images | Labels | Mask boxes | Helmet boxes | Person boxes | Vest boxes |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for name,split in facts['dataset_splits'].items():lines.append('| '+name+' | '+' | '.join(str(v) for v in [split['images'],split['labels'],*split['class_box_counts'].values()])+' |')
lines+=['','The saved augmentation report separately states 12092 train, 1511 validation and 1512 test images. These are historical report values, not a fresh scan of an augmented dataset. Its full text and the pooling-script lines/hashes are saved in project-facts.json. Test/validation images entered the augmentation pool: leakage-free evaluation and a clean retrain remain pending.','','## Training artifact facts','','The same fact-extraction command read `training_artifacts/yolov8s/args.yaml` and `results.csv` without executing training code. Args requested 100 epochs, batch 16, image size 640, SGD, seed 42 and device 0. The configured resume/model path is recorded in the saved args text. There are 99 CSV rows, ending at epoch 99. Do not claim 100 completed epochs or independently verified GPU hardware.','','| Logged epoch | Precision(B) | Recall(B) | mAP50(B) | mAP50-95(B) |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for run in facts['training_runs']:
 row=run.get('last_row')
 if row:lines.append('| '+' | '.join(row[k] for k in ['epoch','metrics/precision(B)','metrics/recall(B)','metrics/mAP50(B)','metrics/mAP50-95(B)'])+' |')
lines+=['','These are historical validation-log numbers. They are not current ONNX test metrics, not validated worker-compliance accuracy, and not leakage-free generalization evidence. No retraining or model swap occurred.','','## Current ONNX evaluation','','Commands: `python -B backend/tools/evaluate_onnx.py --split <test-or-valid> --output <output>`. Exact executable/paths are in each saved metrics.json. Confidence 0.50 and NMS IoU 0.45 were retained. AP uses 101 recall samples at IoU .50:.05:.95 **only over retained detections**; it is threshold-truncated, not full-score COCO/Ultralytics AP. Both splits carry the leakage warning.','','| Split / class | Precision | Recall | AP50, thresholded | AP50-95, thresholded |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for split in ['test','valid']:
 result=json.loads((ROOT/f'docs/evidence/phase3/{split}/metrics.json').read_text())
 for name,row in result['per_class'].items():lines.append('| '+split+' / '+name+' | '+' | '.join(f'{row[k]:.5f}' for k in ['precision','recall','ap50','ap50_95'])+' |')
lines+=['','PR curves, confusion matrices, per-image predictions and source hashes are stored alongside metrics.json. Person misses are a major end-to-end limitation.','','## Worker evaluation','','`python -B backend/tools/violation_eval.py --predictions <split/predictions.json> --output <workers-output>` reran actual association/face logic using hash-verified detector outputs. Box-based ground truth is an exploratory geometric proxy that assumes complete annotation. Both splits yielded zero confirmed fully compliant workers; full compliance precision/recall is null. Most absent-mask truth is unknown without independent visible-face labels. Do not present proxy violation scores as validated safety accuracy.','','## Measured CPU pipeline','','Command/method: `docs/evidence/phase2/benchmark/benchmark.json`, produced by `backend/tools/benchmark.py`. One warm-up excluded; paced video replay, actual model/rules/JPEG and immediate local ACK sink. No DB or transport.','','| Measurement | Value |','|---|---:|',f"| Mean detector ms | {benchmark['detector_ms']['mean']:.3f} |",f"| Delivered FPS | {benchmark['delivered_fps']:.3f} |",f"| Mean frame age ms | {benchmark['frame_age_ms']['mean']:.3f} |",f"| Mean preview MIME/attachment ms | {benchmark['preview_alert_ms']['mean']:.3f} |",'','Delivered FPS reuses cached detections and does not equal fresh detection FPS. Local frame age excludes browser/network/camera buffering. No GPU hardware performance or real email latency was measured.','','## QA and deployment evidence','','Phase test commands/output: `docs/evidence/phase1` through `phase5`. Final browser matrix and screenshots: `docs/qa-report.md`, `docs/screenshots/`. Clean Python 3.14 venv install/pip check: `docs/evidence/phase1/pip-install-report.json` and environment-check.log. Single-admin access, encrypted camera credentials, preview guards, review/archive and real observation denominators have isolated/browser coverage as stated there. Physical webcam, native Linux hardware, real SMTP/Twilio, full-score AP and independently labeled compliance evaluation remain unverified.','','## Defense wording','','Say: "The implemented system supports reviewable live/upload PPE monitoring. Its observed detector and exploratory worker results are provisional because of split leakage and incomplete worker/face ground truth." Explain unknown mask states, person misses, position cooldown limitations and the human review workflow. Avoid claiming site-wide unique-worker compliance, guaranteed alerts, certified safety performance, or generalization from the leaked split.']
(ROOT/'docs/final-year-report-notes.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
